---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import { REPO, REQUEST_URL } from "../data/catalogue";
---
<Base
  page="about"
  title="About Free the Tools, a Sapience Design initiative"
  description="Why Free the Tools exists, how the tools keep your files on your device, and how anyone can add the next one. An open-source initiative by Sapience Design."
  jsonLd={{ "@type": "AboutPage", name: "About Free the Tools", url: "https://freethetools.com/about/" }}
>
  <div class="page narrow about">
    <a class="back" href="/"><Icon name="caret-left" />All tools</a>
    <div class="intro">
      <h1 class="h1">About Free the Tools</h1>
      <div class="belief">
        <p>Everyday tools shouldn't cost money.</p>
        <p>They shouldn't come with ads.</p>
        <p>They shouldn't put your files at risk.</p>
        <p>They shouldn't be hard to find.</p>
        <p class="belief-end">So here they are: one place, every tool, free for everyone.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="lede">Small tools for everyday jobs, like making a PDF smaller or turning a photo into a JPG. Each one works inside your browser, so your files stay on your device.</p>
    </div>

    <dl class="card pledge">
      <div><dt>Nothing is uploaded</dt><dd>The tools run on your own device. Every page carries a security policy that stops it sending data to any other server, and our automated tests fail if one tries.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>No account</dt><dd>We don't ask who you are. No cookies, no IDs, no analytics scripts. We count visits and how often each tool is used, never what you put into it. <a href="/stats/">See exactly what's counted.</a></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Free to use</dt><dd>No limits, no watermarks, no ads and no paid version.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Open source</dt><dd>The code is public under AGPL-3.0, so anyone can check what each tool does, run it themselves or improve it.</dd></div>
    </dl>

    <a class="card how-link" href="/how-it-works/">
      <span><b>How it works, and how to check it yourself</b>What stays on your device, exactly what we send, and what this browser stores.</span>
      <Icon name="arrow-right" />
    </a>

    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn" href={REQUEST_URL}><Icon name="plus" />Suggest a tool</a>
      <a class="btn line" href="mailto:hello@freethetools.com">Contact us</a>
    </div>

    <section aria-labelledby="how-h">
      <h2 class="h2" id="how-h">How a tool gets here</h2>
      <ol class="steps-list">
        <li>Someone <a href={REQUEST_URL}>suggests a tool</a> on GitHub. Others vote with a 👍.</li>
        <li>A maintainer accepts it and marks it wanted.</li>
        <li>A contributor builds it from the template and opens a pull request.</li>
        <li>Automated checks run and a maintainer reviews it.</li>
        <li>Once merged, it goes live here with the builder's name on it.</li>
      </ol>
      <p><a class="btn line small" href={`${REPO}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>Build a tool</a></p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="who-h">
      <h2 class="h2" id="who-h">Who is behind it</h2>
      <p>Free the Tools is an initiative of <a href="https://sapience.design">Sapience Design</a>, a product design studio. Sapience Design maintains the project, reviews contributions and pays for the domain. Hosting is free on Cloudflare.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="ai-h">
      <h2 class="h2" id="ai-h">Works with AI assistants</h2>
      <p>Claude, Cursor and other AI assistants can use these tools instead of installing software. The <code class="mono">freethetools</code> package runs the same tools on your own computer, so an assistant can compress, merge or convert your files without sending them anywhere. It is free, with no account and no login: there is nothing to sign in to, because nothing runs on our servers. In Claude Code, one command sets it up: <code class="mono">claude mcp add freethetools -- npx -y freethetools mcp</code>. The package is on <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/freethetools">npm</a> and in the official <a href="https://registry.modelcontextprotocol.io/">MCP Registry</a>, as <code class="mono">io.github.sapience-design/freethetools</code>, so assistants that look tools up there can find it. In browsers that support WebMCP, an assistant can use the tools right on the page. Every job an assistant does is recorded in your <a href="/library/">library</a>, on your device, so you can see what it did and get the results again.</p>
      <p>There is no hosted version for assistants, because that would mean uploading your files. <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/docs/how-to/use-with-ai.md`}>Setup for each assistant.</a></p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="browser-h">
      <h2 class="h2" id="browser-h">How much can a browser do?</h2>
      <p>More than most people expect. Ghostscript, the engine behind professional PDF software, runs inside the page as WebAssembly. So do qpdf, the PDF library pdf-lib, and the image codecs, and every tool keeps working offline once you have opened it. Every year the gap between "needs a server" and "runs on your device" gets smaller, and we add tools as it closes.</p>
      <p>Next on the list: files bigger than your memory, text recognition for scans, translation, and pages in more languages. Jobs that still need a server, such as rebuilding a PDF as an editable Word file, wait until a browser engine can do them. We do not add a server to get there.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="dev-h">
      <h2 class="h2" id="dev-h">For developers</h2>
      <p>The full catalogue is available as JSON at <a href="/api/tools.json" class="mono">/api/tools.json</a>, described by an <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/openapi.yaml`}>OpenAPI file</a>, with a plain-text summary for language models at <a href="/llms.txt" class="mono">/llms.txt</a> and every tool's details at <a href="/llms-full.txt" class="mono">/llms-full.txt</a>. Each tool's logic lives in a plain module you can run yourself.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="lic-h">
      <h2 class="h2" id="lic-h">Licence and name</h2>
      <p>The code is AGPL-3.0, copyright Sapience Design and contributors. The Free the Tools name and the Sapience name and logo are trademarks and are not covered by the code licence. The tools are provided as they are, without warranty, as the AGPL says. Check the output yourself before relying on it. See <a href="/licenses/">licences</a> and <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/TRADEMARKS.md`}>trademarks</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="sec-h">
      <h2 class="h2" id="sec-h">Security</h2>
      <p>Found a vulnerability? Please report it privately through <a href={`${REPO}/security/advisories/new`}>GitHub's private reporting</a>, not in a public issue. Our <a href={`${REPO}/security/policy`}>security policy</a> explains what happens next.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about { display: grid; gap: 28px; }
  .intro { display: grid; gap: 20px; }
  .belief { display: grid; gap: 2px; }
  .belief p { margin: 0; font-family: var(--display); font-size: clamp(20px, 1rem + 0.8vw, 24px); line-height: 1.3; color: var(--soft); }
  .belief .belief-end { margin-top: 10px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); }
  .pledge { margin: 0; }
  .how-link { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 16px; padding: 16px 18px; color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; }
  .how-link span { display: grid; gap: 2px; flex: 1; color: var(--soft); }
  .how-link b { color: var(--ink); }
  .how-link :global(.ic) { font-size: 20px; flex: none; }
  .how-link:hover { border-color: var(--edge); }
  .pledge div { display: grid; gap: 4px; padding: 16px 18px; }
  .pledge div + div { border-top: 1px solid var(--hair); }
  .pledge dt { font-weight: 700; }
  .pledge dd { margin: 0; color: var(--soft); }
  .pledge a, section a:not(.btn) { color: var(--ink); }
  section { display: grid; gap: 10px; padding-top: 8px; }
  section p { color: var(--soft); }
  .steps-list { margin: 0; padding-left: 22px; display: grid; gap: 6px; color: var(--soft); }
</style>
